{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489457-sc-2e-enemies-balancing-help","id":1489457,"title":"[Sc 2E] Enemies balancing help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-08T01:49:26-07:00","id":1489457,"title":"[Sc 2E] Enemies balancing help","content":"Could not find similar topic, so starting one...<br /> <br /> Is SWAT team ( from Origin) a real danger for Legend 1 PC with extra 20-40 XP each? Let's say 2 SWAT per 1 Scion? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T13:54:26-07:00","id":1489500,"title":"","content":"There's no way to answer that in a vacuum... Scion isn't D&amp;D where Legend can be compared to an obstacle's Challenge Rating to know have a strong clue about how well the PCs will do against it. While IME even at Legend 1 a SWAT team isn't really going to be a big challenge, that's mostly because my groups tend to either be a group of generalists where everyone has decent pools in most situations and then the PCs use the teamwork bonuses in the game that vastly exceeding what the antagonists get, or each PC is a specialist in a different area and then in combat the combat specialist will dispatch enemies quickly enough and the rest of the Band focuses on support and so on the maximize that/minimize damage done to the PCs.<br /> <br /> But people could make a band of divinely awesome smart PCs where they can Sherlock Holmes their way through most things, but nobody's invested enough in combat to actually beat a SWAT team reliably at Legend 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T17:19:34-07:00","id":1489512,"title":"","content":"Agreed with Heavy Arms. You will need keep track of the PCs stats when planning encounters. There are legend 1 characters who can wipe the floor them them, and those who would be challenged by an annoyed 7th grader.I have my players keep their sheets on a dropbox for me to consult, but you should get a feel for them over time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T18:43:44-07:00","id":1489520,"title":"","content":"There's also how familiar the players are with the system. How good they are with handling threshold successes, Bonds, and the specifics of combat stunts can have a big impact on character success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T00:56:04-07:00","id":1489853,"title":"","content":"I got advice to use 2 Rival antagonists per Scion PC to make tough encounter for them. Here are first take on the stats for this enemies from SWAT.<br /> <br /> <b>Anti-Mythical SWAT ( Hero Tier )</b><br /> <br /> A real challenge for aspiring Scions, this SWAT units are specially trained to fight with Heroes on instances when law don\u2019t agree with Pantheons interests. They are more driven in training than normal SWAT units ( see <b>Scion Origin </b>p. 154 ) just to catch Children of the Gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Archetype</b>: Rival<br /> <b>Qualities:</b> Group Tactics ( <b>Origin</b> p. 147 ), Heavily Armored ( +2 Def, +1 Armour )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Spray n\u2019 Pray (H&amp;K submachine gun), Dread Gaze (Flashbang grenades)<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To take down the target with extreme prejudice<br /> <b>Primary Pool:</b> 9 (Combat, Sniping, Athletics)<br /> <b>Secondary Pool:</b> 7 (Demolitions, Alertness)<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 5<br /> <b>Health:</b> 3<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 (5)<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Extras:</b> +2 Enhancement for Stunts other than Inflict Damage<br /> <br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Close Combat Training<br /> <b>Submachine Gun</b> ( H&amp;K submachine ) \u2013 Enhancement 2, Automatic (2), Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Ranged (0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-12-2022, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T14:21:46-07:00","id":1490063,"title":"","content":"The AM SWAT looks pretty good.<br /> <br /> A problem I've run into with Keen-Eyed Predator can derail potential ambush or surprises like nothing else. I've got a over arching Titan faction that's turned into the long running antagonists for the players from the Aesir Pantheon that I started during Origin and have rolled into my Hero campaign (The Harbingers of Raganrok, a frightening competent organization of disaffected veterans &amp; supporters fallen under the sway of the Aesir Titans). <br /> <br /> The issue is I have a player who is a bit of a pain as they use Keen Eyed Predator a lot and it kills game flow as they roll pretty well and ask the questions presented. Which kills any potential for surprise. Most of the group is not as combat heavy, so on the one hand it's good. But it does kill Mystery. And since I am leaning on Myth, losing mystery kind of hurts.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for helping dial this back a bit. I've gotten them to Legend 2 as of last session, and they are creeping around the edges of Hel, having just gotten past M\u00f3\u00f0gu\u00f0r to travel the bridge Gjallarbru to got to...Hel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T20:20:43-07:00","id":1490091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheWanderingJewels</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489457-sc-2e-enemies-balancing-help?p=1490063#post1490063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The AM SWAT looks pretty good.<br /> <br /> A problem I've run into with Keen-Eyed Predator can derail potential ambush or surprises like nothing else. I've got a over arching Titan faction that's turned into the long running antagonists for the players from the Aesir Pantheon that I started during Origin and have rolled into my Hero campaign (The Harbingers of Raganrok, a frightening competent organization of disaffected veterans &amp; supporters fallen under the sway of the Aesir Titans).<br /> <br /> The issue is I have a player who is a bit of a pain as they use Keen Eyed Predator a lot and it kills game flow as they roll pretty well and ask the questions presented. Which kills any potential for surprise. Most of the group is not as combat heavy, so on the one hand it's good. But it does kill Mystery. And since I am leaning on Myth, losing mystery kind of hurts.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for helping dial this back a bit. I've gotten them to Legend 2 as of last session, and they are creeping around the edges of Hel, having just gotten past M\u00f3\u00f0gu\u00f0r to travel the bridge Gjallarbru to got to...Hel.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first recommendation is discuss the matter with the group. How do you feel about it? If you have a group who considers the PC an MVP and like how it goes, then you may need to adapt. If the Player is annoying everyone who wants to have more mystery, they should adapt. IME, the players often like having the ability to prep like that, but obviously not always and sometimes people dislike it. As a player, I like having warning, and am known for frontloading on perceptive abilities. I usually GM, and I adapt. But within the group we talk about it. So I guess number one what does everyone want.<br /> <br /> A compromise might be only having it work in either natural or urban environs, depending on the PCs style, Maybe not detect enemies of greater tier. Either change I would discuss first.<br /> <br /> End of the day, find the pulse of the group, everyone discuss their feelings.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}